WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.723
Energy. Transport. Climate. For more than ten years, Bernie Calderon Magtalas

00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:11.045
has helped the Philippine Government decide which infrastructure investments are worth making.

00:00:12.195 --> 00:00:17.817
He started at the Department of Energy in 2015. Today, he is

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:23.438
a Supervising Economic Development Specialist at the Department of Economy, Planning, and Development.

00:00:24.588 --> 00:00:30.625
Thirty-four infrastructure projects. Fourteen point zero five billion dollars. Airports, roads,

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:36.663
rail, energy, and ports, all appraised under the ICC review framework.

00:00:37.813 --> 00:00:41.557
Fifteen development partner programs. Forty-eight bills, laws,

00:00:41.557 --> 00:00:45.301
and policies. And eight national boards advised.

00:00:46.451 --> 00:00:51.784
He built the Philippines' first Regional Infrastructure Development Index, and a model that

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:57.117
ranked two hundred and seven projects in a one hundred seventy-six billion dollar pipeline.

00:00:58.267 --> 00:01:05.510
He is part of SIPA's Regional Knowledge Network on Sustainable Infrastructure, run by the

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:12.753
Asian Institute of Technology, UNDP, and the OECD, linking policymakers and experts across Southeast Asia.

00:01:13.903 --> 00:01:21.071
A Waseda University graduate and JICA scholar, he is also a World Energy Council Future Energy Leader.

00:01:22.221 --> 00:01:26.573
See the full portfolio at bcmagtalas.github.io/Career-Portfolio.
